   "html": "<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\">\n<title>Makerspace Colour</title>\n<script type=\"application/json\" id=\"sp-scheme\">\n{\n \"format\": \"sp-scheme-package\",\n \"spScheme\": \"2.0\",\n \"survey\": {\n  \"title\": \"Makerspace Colour Preference and Comfort\",\n  \"description\": \"Faithful replication with the original images: 12 rendered views of a generic makerspace interior (white curved walls with round niches, white seating) whose carpet and niche colour takes one of four hue conditions of the paper's HSL hue series, A8 (blue) and A5 (red), rated highest in the laboratory experiment, and A3 (green) and A7 (purple), rated lower; each hue is shown from three viewpoints (eye level, high-angle overview, wide-angle perspective). Participants imagine entering the space to carry out a semester-long innovation project. Each of the 12 images is shown in random order after a 2 s grey screen for 8 s, and is then rated on two 5-point scales, Preference and Comfort. Age and gender are asked at the end. Rebuilt from Yu, Li & Tang (2026), Contextual decoupling in color preference: multimodal evidence from spatial evaluation in makerspaces, Frontiers in Psychology 17: 1826920 (Experiment 3 viewpoint validation, 68 participants), with the renders cropped from its Figure 4 (CC BY 4.0). Image ids: hue_view, e.g. A8_eye, A5_high, A3_wide. Analysis as in the paper: mean Preference and Comfort per hue and viewpoint, and rank-order stability against the laboratory means (Spearman's rho); the paper found A8 and A5 rated near the top of the scale (above 4) from all three viewpoints and A3 and A7 clearly lower (about 2.2-2.5), so the hue ranking did not depend on one camera angle. Differences from the original study: (1) only the viewpoint validation is rebuilt; the 21 photo-based hue and saturation images of Experiments 2-3 are not used because the published figure prints condition labels on them, and the Munsell chip task (Experiment 1), eye tracking and pupillometry are not included; (2) the paper says this phase used the same rating criteria but not its timing, so the 2 s grey screen and 8 s viewing follow the laboratory procedure of Experiment 2; (3) the paper does not print the question wording or scale labels, so the instruction text, question stems and anchors (1 = not at all, 5 = very much) are ours; (4) the age and gender questions are ours; the paper's laboratory participants were Chinese university students, here anyone can take part; (5) the renders are the figure copies (about 500 px wide).\",\n  \"locale\": \"en\",\n  \"mediaFolders\": [\n   \"rooms\"\n  ],\n  \"pages\": [\n   {\n    \"name\": \"start\",\n    \"elements\": [\n     {\n      \"type\": \"consent\",\n      \"name\": \"consent\",\n      \"title\": \"I agree to take part. Participation is voluntary and my answers are recorded anonymously for research.\",\n      \"isRequired\": true,\n      \"labelTrue\": \"I agree\",\n      \"labelFalse\": \"I do not agree\"\n     }\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"name\": \"images\",\n    \"elements\": [\n     {\n      \"type\": \"matrix\",\n      \"name\": \"rating\",\n      \"title\": \"Imagine working in this space on a long project.\",\n      \"isRequired\": true,\n      \"rows\": [\n       {\n        \"value\": \"preference\",\n        \"text\": \"How much do you like this space? (Preference)\"\n       },\n       {\n        \"value\": \"comfort\",\n        \"text\": \"How comfortable would this space be for sustained work? (Comfort)\"\n       }\n      ],\n      \"columns\": [\n       {\n        \"value\": 1,\n        \"text\": \"1\"\n       },\n       {\n        \"value\": 2,\n        \"text\": \"2\"\n       },\n       {\n        \"value\": 3,\n        \"text\": \"3\"\n       },\n       {\n        \"value\": 4,\n        \"text\": \"4\"\n       },\n       {\n        \"value\": 5,\n        \"text\": \"5\"\n       }\n      ],\n      \"description\": \"5-point scales, 1 = not at all, 5 = very much. Keyed by image id (A8/A5/A3/A7 x eye/high/wide).\"\n     }\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"name\": \"about\",\n    \"elements\": [\n     {\n      \"type\": \"text\",\n      \"inputType\": \"number\",\n      \"name\": \"age\",\n      \"title\": \"How old are you?\",\n      \"isRequired\": true,\n      \"min\": 16,\n      \"max\": 110\n     },\n     {\n      \"type\": \"radiogroup\",\n      \"name\": \"gender\",\n      \"title\": \"Gender\",\n      \"isRequired\": true,\n      \"choices\": [\n       {\n        \"value\": \"female\",\n        \"text\": \"Female\"\n       },\n       {\n        \"value\": \"male\",\n        \"text\": \"Male\"\n       },\n       {\n        \"value\": \"other\",\n        \"text\": \"Other / prefer not to say\"\n       }\n      ]\n     }\n    ]\n   }\n  ]\n }\n}\n</script>\n<script type=\"application/json\" id=\"makerspace-colour-original\">{\"source\": \"Yu, Li & Tang (2026) Frontiers in Psychology 17: 1826920\", \"phase\": \"Experiment 3 viewpoint validation\", \"n\": 68, \"hues\": {\"A8\": \"HSL hue -120 (blue)\", \"A5\": \"HSL hue +30 (red)\", \"A3\": \"HSL hue 180 (green)\", \"A7\": \"HSL hue -30 (purple)\"}, \"lab_means_exp2\": {\"A5\": {\"preference\": 3.42, \"comfort\": 3.33}, \"A8\": {\"preference\": 3.74, \"comfort\": 3.63}}, \"results\": \"A8 and A5 above 4 across viewpoints; A3 about 2.15-2.19, A7 about 2.35-2.5\"}</script>\n<style>\n:root{--bg:#f0f1f4;--card:#fff;--ink:#1c1f26;--muted:#5a6070;--accent:#3b5bab;--line:#d9dce4;--warn:#b3261e;--sel:#e2e8f6}\n*{box-sizing:border-box}html,body{margin:0;background:var(--bg);color:var(--ink);font:17px/1.5 system-ui,-apple-system,\"Segoe UI\",Roboto,sans-serif}\nmain{max-width:820px;margin:0 auto;padding:22px 16px 40px}\nh1{font-size:1.5rem;margin:0 0 8px}h2{font-size:1.15rem;margin:0 0 8px}p{margin:0 0 12px;color:var(--muted)}\n.card{background:var(--card);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:14px;padding:18px;margin-top:14px}\n.btn{appearance:none;border:0;border-radius:10px;padding:13px 20px;font:inherit;font-weight:600;cursor:pointer;background:var(--accent);color:#fff}\n.btn:disabled{opacity:.35;cursor:not-allowed}\n.prog{font-size:.88rem;color:var(--muted);margin-bottom:8px}\n.ins{color:var(--ink)}\n.view{position:fixed;inset:0;background:#808080;display:flex;flex-direction:column;align-items:center;justify-content:center;z-index:5;gap:12px}\n.view img{width:100vw;height:auto;max-height:88vh;object-fit:contain;display:block}\n.view .t{color:#eee;font-size:.85rem;min-height:1.2em}\n.pic img{width:100%;max-height:40vh;object-fit:contain;display:block;border-radius:8px;background:#ddd}\n.it{padding:9px 0;border-top:1px solid var(--line)}\n.it .an{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;font-size:.95rem;margin-bottom:4px}\n.it .o{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(5,1fr);gap:3px}\n.it label{display:flex;flex-direction:column;align-items:center;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:8px;padding:3px 0;cursor:pointer;font-size:.8rem;color:var(--muted)}\n.it label:has(input:checked){background:var(--sel);border-color:var(--accent);color:var(--ink)}\n.it input{margin:0 0 1px}\n.it.miss .o{outline:2px solid var(--warn);outline-offset:2px;border-radius:8px}\nlabel.opt{display:flex;gap:10px;align-items:center;padding:8px 12px;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:10px;margin-top:6px;cursor:pointer}\n.f{margin-top:16px}.f:first-child{margin-top:0}\ninput[type=number]{font:inherit;padding:8px 10px;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:8px;width:110px}\n.err{color:var(--warn);margin-top:8px;min-height:1.2em}\n.credit{max-width:820px;margin:0 auto;padding:0 16px 24px;font-size:.78rem;color:var(--muted)}\n</style>\n</head>\n<body>\n<main id=\"app\" aria-live=\"polite\"><p>Loading…</p></main>\n<footer class=\"credit\">Images: Yu, Li &amp; Tang (2026), Frontiers in Psychology 17: 1826920, Figure 4 (doi:10.3389/fpsyg.2026.1826920, CC BY 4.0).</footer>\n<script>\n(function(){\n  var KEY='makerspace-colour:state', T={view:window.__VIEWMS||8000,blank:window.__VIEWMS?20:2000};\n  var IDS=[];['A8','A5','A3','A7'].forEach(function(h){['eye','high','wide'].forEach(function(v){IDS.push(h+'_'+v);});});\n  var app=document.getElementById('app'), Q={}, files={}, st=null;\n  function esc(s){return String(s==null?'':s).replace(/[&<>\"]/g,function(c){return {'&':'&amp;','<':'&lt;','>':'&gt;','\"':'&quot;'}[c];});}\n  function err(m){var e=app.querySelector('.err');if(e)e.textContent=m||'';}\n  function ok(r){return !(r&&r.ok===false);}\n  function save(){try{localStorage.setItem(KEY,JSON.stringify(st));}catch(e){}}\n  function send(list,b,next){if(b)b.disabled=true;Promise.all(list).then(function(rs){var bad=rs.filter(function(r){return !ok(r);})[0];if(bad){if(b)b.disabled=false;return err(bad.error);}next();});}\n  function val(name){var x=app.querySelector('input[name=\"'+name+'\"]:checked');return x?x.value:null;}\n  function shuffle(a){a=a.slice();for(var i=a.length-1;i>0;i--){var j=Math.floor(Math.random()*(i+1));var t=a[i];a[i]=a[j];a[j]=t;}return a;}\n  function fresh(){return {step:'intro',order:shuffle(IDS),k:0,phase:'blank'};}\n  function intro(){\n    app.innerHTML='<h1>Makerspace interiors</h1><p>Imagine that you are entering a university makerspace, a shared workshop where you will carry out a semester-long innovation project. You will see '+IDS.length+' pictures of such a space, one at a time: a grey screen for 2 seconds, then the picture for 8 seconds. After each picture, rate how much you like the space and how comfortable it would be for sustained work. It takes about 5 minutes.</p><div class=\"card\"><label class=\"opt\" style=\"margin-top:0\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"ok\"> '+esc(Q.consent.title)+'</label><div style=\"margin-top:16px\"><button class=\"btn\" id=\"go\">Start</button></div><div class=\"err\"></div></div>';\n    document.getElementById('go').onclick=function(){if(!document.getElementById('ok').checked)return err('Consent is needed to continue.');send([SPSite.answer('consent',true)],this,function(){st.step='trial';st.phase='blank';save();route();});};\n  }\n  function timer(ms,label,done){var end=Date.now()+ms,tm=document.getElementById('tm');(function tick(){var s=Math.ceil((end-Date.now())/1000);if(s<=0)return done();if(tm)tm.textContent=label(s);setTimeout(tick,250);})();}\n  function trial(){\n    if(st.k>=st.order.length){st.step='about';save();return route();}\n    var id=st.order[st.k],v=document.createElement('div');v.className='view';app.innerHTML='';app.appendChild(v);\n    if(st.phase==='q')return ask();\n    if(st.phase==='blank'){v.innerHTML='<div class=\"t\" id=\"tm\"></div>';var p=new Image();p.src=files[id].url;return timer(T.blank,function(s){return '';},function(){st.phase='view';save();route();});}\n    v.innerHTML='<img alt=\"Makerspace interior\" src=\"'+esc(files[id].url)+'\"><div class=\"t\" id=\"tm\"></div>';\n    timer(T.view,function(s){return 'Picture '+(st.k+1)+' of '+st.order.length;},function(){st.phase='q';save();route();});\n  }\n  function ask(){\n    var id=st.order[st.k],f=files[id],q=Q.rating;\n    app.innerHTML='<div class=\"prog\">Picture '+(st.k+1)+' of '+st.order.length+'</div><div class=\"card\"><p class=\"ins\" style=\"margin:0 0 6px\">'+esc(q.title)+' Rate the picture you just saw (1 = not at all, 5 = very much).</p>'+(q.rows||[]).map(function(r){var nm='sd__'+r.value;return '<div class=\"it\" data-n=\"'+nm+'\"><div class=\"an\"><span>'+esc(r.text)+'</span></div><div class=\"o\">'+(q.columns||[]).map(function(c){return '<label><input type=\"radio\" name=\"'+nm+'\" value=\"'+c.value+'\">'+c.value+'</label>';}).join('')+'</div></div>';}).join('')+'<div style=\"margin-top:16px\"><button class=\"btn\" id=\"go\">Next</button></div><div class=\"err\"></div></div>';\n    document.getElementById('go').onclick=function(){\n      var out={},miss=0,first=null;\n      (q.rows||[]).forEach(function(r){var nm='sd__'+r.value,x=val(nm),el=app.querySelector('.it[data-n=\"'+nm+'\"]');if(x==null){miss++;el.classList.add('miss');if(!first)first=el;}else{el.classList.remove('miss');out[r.value]=Number(x);}});\n      if(miss){if(first)first.scrollIntoView({block:'center'});return err('Please answer both questions.');}\n      send([SPSite.answer('rating',out,{key:id,shown:[f.name]})],this,function(){st.k++;st.phase='blank';save();route();});\n    };\n  }\n  function about(){\n    app.innerHTML='<h2>About you</h2><div class=\"card\"><div class=\"f\"><b>'+esc(Q.age.title)+'</b><br><input type=\"number\" id=\"age\" min=\"16\" max=\"110\"></div><div class=\"f\"><b>'+esc(Q.gender.title)+'</b>'+(Q.gender.choices||[]).map(function(c){return '<label class=\"opt\"><input type=\"radio\" name=\"gender\" value=\"'+esc(c.value)+'\"> '+esc(c.text)+'</label>';}).join('')+'</div><div style=\"margin-top:16px\"><button class=\"btn\" id=\"go\">Finish</button></div><div class=\"err\"></div></div>';\n    document.getElementById('go').onclick=function(){var age=Number(document.getElementById('age').value),g=val('gender');if(!(age>=16&&age<=110))return err('Please enter your age.');if(!g)return err('Please choose your gender.');\n      send([SPSite.answer('age',age),SPSite.answer('gender',g)],this,function(){st.step='done';save();route();});};\n  }\n  function finish(){\n    app.innerHTML='<h1>Thank you!</h1><div class=\"card\"><p id=\"fin\">Submitting…</p><div class=\"err\"></div></div>';\n    SPSite.complete().then(function(r){if(!ok(r)){err(r.error||'Some answers are missing.');setTimeout(function(){st.step='intro';save();route();},1800);}\n      else{try{localStorage.removeItem(KEY);}catch(e){}var s=document.getElementById('fin');if(s)s.textContent='Your answers are saved.';}});\n  }\n  app.addEventListener('change',function(e){var r=e.target.closest&&e.target.closest('.it');if(r){r.classList.remove('miss');if(!app.querySelector('.it.miss'))err('');}});\n  function route(){var s=st.step;window.scrollTo(0,0);if(s==='trial')return trial();if(s==='about')return about();if(s==='done')return finish();intro();}\n  SPSite.onReady(function(ctx){\n    ['consent','rating','age','gender'].forEach(function(n){Q[n]=SPSite.getQuestion(n)||{};});\n    (SPSite.getMedia('rooms')||[]).forEach(function(f){files[f.name.replace(/\\.[^.]+$/,'')]=f;});\n    var need=IDS.filter(function(k){return !files[k];});\n    if(need.length){app.innerHTML='<h1>Images missing</h1><p>Upload '+need.join(', ')+' (.jpg) to the media folder \"rooms\".</p>';return;}\n    try{st=JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem(KEY));}catch(e){st=null;}\n    var a=(ctx&&ctx.answers)||{};\n    if(!(st&&st.order)||a.consent!==true)st=fresh();\n    save();route();\n  });\n})();\n</script>\n</body>\n</html>\n",
